{
  "info": {
    "name": "Claim Provenance API",
    "description": "Manual test collection for the /v1/analyze endpoint.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Import this file into Postman (File → Import → drag `postman_collection.json`).\n2. Open the collection's **Variables** tab and set:\n   - `baseUrl` — e.g. `http://localhost:8787` for local dev.\n   - `bearerToken` — leave empty if backend has `REQUIRE_AUTH=false` and you want to test the anonymous path. Set to one of your `API_KEYS` tokens otherwise.\n3. Make sure the backend is running (`cd backend && npm run start`).\n4. Run requests individually, or use the **Run collection** button to execute the whole suite end-to-end.\n\nThe collection includes assertions on each request — open the **Test Results** tab after running to see what passed/failed.\n\n## See also\n\n- [`Docs/API.md`](API.md) — prose reference\n- [`backend/openapi.yaml`](../backend/openapi.yaml) — machine-readable spec\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8787",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "bearerToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Leave empty to call as the anonymous principal (only works when REQUIRE_AUTH=false). Otherwise set to one of the tokens declared in API_KEYS."
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health & discovery",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /healthz",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/healthz",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["healthz"]
            },
            "description": "Unauthenticated probe. Reports provider, key presence, auth posture, and cache size."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has ok=true', () => pm.expect(j.ok).to.equal(true));",
                  "pm.test('Reports provider', () => pm.expect(j.provider).to.be.oneOf(['anthropic', 'azure_openai']));",
                  "pm.test('Reports require_auth', () => pm.expect(j).to.have.property('require_auth'));",
                  "pm.test('Reports api_keys_loaded', () => pm.expect(j.api_keys_loaded).to.be.a('number'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/openapi.yaml",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/openapi.yaml",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "openapi.yaml"]
            },
            "description": "OpenAPI 3.1 spec for the API. Also available at `/openapi.yaml` (same file)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Returns YAML', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.match(/yaml/));",
                  "pm.test('Body starts with openapi: 3', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.match(/^openapi:\\s+3/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "/v1/analyze — happy paths",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/analyze — first call (cold, X-Cache: miss)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/wfh-2024\",\n  \"title\": \"What Four Years of Remote-Work Data Actually Tell Us\",\n  \"page_text\": \"According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, 27 percent of U.S. employees worked from home at least one day per week in 2023. Microsoft's 2023 Work Trend Index, a survey of 31,000 workers across 31 countries, found that 64 percent of respondents said workplace flexibility had improved their work-life balance.\",\n  \"page_links\": [\n    {\n      \"href\": \"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/atus.t05.htm\",\n      \"anchor_text\": \"U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics\",\n      \"near_text\": \"According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, 27 percent of U.S. employees worked from home at least one day per week in 2023.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"href\": \"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/worklab/work-trend-index/\",\n      \"anchor_text\": \"Microsoft's 2023 Work Trend Index\",\n      \"near_text\": \"Microsoft's 2023 Work Trend Index, a survey of 31,000 workers across 31 countries, found that 64 percent\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/analyze",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "analyze"]
            },
            "description": "Sends a small WFH article with two real inline citations (BLS and Microsoft Work Trend Index). Expect ~15-30s on first call. The response is cached by sha256(url + page_text); the next request reuses the same body to demonstrate `X-Cache: hit`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('X-Request-Id header present', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id')).to.match(/^req_/));",
                  "pm.test('X-Cache: miss on first call', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Cache')).to.equal('miss'));",
                  "pm.test('X-RateLimit headers present', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Limit')).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Remaining')).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response shape matches AnalyzeResponse', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('claims').that.is.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('chains').that.is.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('meta');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('request_id');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('fallback_uses').that.is.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('claims[i] aligns with chains[i]', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.claims.length).to.equal(j.chains.length);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Each chain has the required taxonomy fields', () => {",
                  "  for (const ch of j.chains) {",
                  "    pm.expect(ch.status).to.be.oneOf(['primary', 'direct_cited', 'indirect_cited', 'stale_cited', 'circular', 'untraceable']);",
                  "    pm.expect(ch.hop_count).to.be.a('number');",
                  "    pm.expect(ch.nodes).to.be.an('array');",
                  "    pm.expect(ch.notes).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  }",
                  "});",
                  "// Stash the request_id and cache key so the next request can verify cache reuse",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lastRequestId', j.request_id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/analyze — same body (warm, X-Cache: hit)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/wfh-2024\",\n  \"title\": \"What Four Years of Remote-Work Data Actually Tell Us\",\n  \"page_text\": \"According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, 27 percent of U.S. employees worked from home at least one day per week in 2023. Microsoft's 2023 Work Trend Index, a survey of 31,000 workers across 31 countries, found that 64 percent of respondents said workplace flexibility had improved their work-life balance.\",\n  \"page_links\": [\n    {\n      \"href\": \"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/atus.t05.htm\",\n      \"anchor_text\": \"U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics\",\n      \"near_text\": \"According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, 27 percent of U.S. employees worked from home at least one day per week in 2023.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"href\": \"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/worklab/work-trend-index/\",\n      \"anchor_text\": \"Microsoft's 2023 Work Trend Index\",\n      \"near_text\": \"Microsoft's 2023 Work Trend Index, a survey of 31,000 workers across 31 countries, found that 64 percent\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/analyze",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "analyze"]
            },
            "description": "Same body as the previous request. The LRU cache is keyed by sha256(url + page_text), so this should return in ~3ms with `X-Cache: hit`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('X-Cache: hit', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Cache')).to.equal('hit'));",
                  "pm.test('Response time < 200ms', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(200));",
                  "pm.test('X-Request-Id is a NEW id (cache hits get fresh request_ids)', () => {",
                  "  const newId = pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id');",
                  "  const oldId = pm.collectionVariables.get('lastRequestId');",
                  "  pm.expect(newId).to.not.equal(oldId);",
                  "});",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Body claim count matches the cold call', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.claims.length).to.equal(j.chains.length);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/analyze — synthetic untraceable case",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/midmarket-ai\",\n  \"title\": \"Why Mid-Market Companies Are Outpacing the Fortune 500 on AI\",\n  \"page_text\": \"A 2024 BridgeWater Research survey of 1,400 IT directors found that 67 percent of mid-market firms now have at least one generative AI deployment in production, compared to just 41 percent at Fortune 500 companies. Industry analysts at Forrester now estimate that mid-market firms will spend an aggregate $34 billion on AI tools in 2025.\",\n  \"page_links\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/analyze",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "analyze"]
            },
            "description": "Synthetic article with two fabricated-source claims (BridgeWater Research and a specific Forrester forecast). Expect both to classify as `untraceable` after the false-untraceable retry path also returns nothing. Demonstrates the `fallback_uses` counter — both claims should trigger the retry."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('All chains classified as untraceable', () => {",
                  "  for (const ch of j.chains) pm.expect(ch.status).to.equal('untraceable');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('fallback_uses > 0 (retry fired on every untraceable claim)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.fallback_uses).to.be.greaterThan(0);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('hop_count is -1 for untraceable', () => {",
                  "  for (const ch of j.chains) pm.expect(ch.hop_count).to.equal(-1);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "/v1/analyze — error cases",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "400 — missing page_text",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/x\",\n  \"title\": \"x\",\n  \"page_links\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/analyze",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "analyze"]
            },
            "description": "Missing required `page_text` field. Expect a 400 with the validation message."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('error: invalid_request', () => pm.expect(j.error).to.equal('invalid_request'));",
                  "pm.test('Message names the missing field', () => pm.expect(j.message).to.match(/page_text/));",
                  "pm.test('Includes request_id for support', () => pm.expect(j.request_id).to.match(/^req_/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "401 — invalid bearer token",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "definitely_not_a_real_token", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/x\",\n  \"title\": \"x\",\n  \"page_text\": \"x\",\n  \"page_links\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/analyze",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "analyze"]
            },
            "description": "Sends a bogus bearer token. Expect 401 `invalid_token` regardless of the server's REQUIRE_AUTH setting (a present-but-wrong token is always rejected)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('error: invalid_token', () => pm.expect(j.error).to.equal('invalid_token'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "401 — missing auth (only fires when REQUIRE_AUTH=true)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/x\",\n  \"title\": \"x\",\n  \"page_text\": \"x\",\n  \"page_links\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/analyze",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "analyze"]
            },
            "description": "No auth header. When `REQUIRE_AUTH=true` on the server: 401 `missing_auth`. When `REQUIRE_AUTH=false`: 200, attributed to the anonymous principal. The test below auto-detects which mode is active by hitting /healthz first."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Probe /healthz to find out whether REQUIRE_AUTH is on, then store the answer.",
                  "pm.sendRequest({",
                  "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/healthz',",
                  "  method: 'GET'",
                  "}, (err, resp) => {",
                  "  if (err) return;",
                  "  const j = resp.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('requireAuth', String(j.require_auth));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const requireAuth = pm.collectionVariables.get('requireAuth') === 'true';",
                  "if (requireAuth) {",
                  "  pm.test('REQUIRE_AUTH=true → 401 missing_auth', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.equal('missing_auth');",
                  "  });",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('REQUIRE_AUTH=false → 200 anonymous (or other valid status)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 400, 429, 500]);",
                  "  });",
                  "  pm.test.skip('Skipped: this assertion only runs when REQUIRE_AUTH=true');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
